# Oracle Cloud's settings (`metacomputer vm create NAME --on oci` writes them to config/vms/NAME.env), as comments:
# nothing here is read as a setting; config/defaults.env has the defaults every computer shares. Its docs: docs/remote.md, Oracle Cloud (OCI).
#   PLACE=oci, PROVIDER=oci, TRANSPORT=ssh
#   SIZE                     arm-2x12 (the default), arm-1x6, x86-1x8, x86-2x8, x86-micro
#   IDLE_STOP                minutes unused before it powers itself off (15; off: never). Oracle still counts it as
#                            running, and bills a billed size, until it's stopped there (metacomputer stop)
#   EGRESS                   internet or off: its own firewall, and its network security group outside it
# This checkout's settings (config/local.env), copied into a new computer's file:
#   OCI_PYTHON               a Python with Oracle's SDK (pip install oci), which lib/remote.py runs with
# Its credentials, only from the environment of the command that needs them (never a file):
#   OCI_USER, OCI_TENANCY, OCI_FINGERPRINT, OCI_REGION, OCI_API_KEY_PEM (the PEM text), OCI_COMPARTMENT
